  "body": "USDM uses 6 decimals because it is minted 1:1 against USDC. sUSDM is an ERC4626 vault over USDM and sets `_decimalsOffset()` to 6.\n\nERC4626 uses this offset in share conversion:\n\n```solidity\nfunction previewDeposit(uint256 assets) public view virtual returns (uint256) {\n    return _convertToShares(assets, Math.Rounding.Floor);\n}\n\nfunction _convertToShares(uint256 assets, Math.Rounding rounding) internal view virtual returns (uint256) {\n    return assets.mulDiv(totalSupply() + 10 ** _decimalsOffset(), totalAssets() + 1, rounding);\n}\n```\n\nTherefore, with a 6-decimal asset and a 6-decimal offset, sUSDM shares are 12-decimal shares. For example, depositing `1e6` USDM mints `1e12` sUSDM.\n\nThis also matches the [docs](https://doc.monetrix.xyz/guide/faq):\n\n> USDM: 6 decimals (matches USDC). sUSDM: 12 decimals.\n\nHowever, the current sUSDM implementation overrides `decimals()` to return 6:\n\n```solidity\nfunction decimals() public pure override returns (uint8) {\n    return 6;\n}\n```\n\nAs a result, sUSDM share math uses 12 decimals, while the ERC20 metadata reports 6 decimals. External integrations and protocols relying on `decimals()` may value sUSDM balances incorrectly by a factor of `1e6`.\n\n## Impact\n\nFor example, an external protocol interacting with sUSDM may want to convert an sUSDM balance to USDC. The calculation may look like this:\n\n`sUSDM amount * price * 10 ** usdc.decimals() / (10 ** susdm.decimals() * price offset)`\n\nFor simplicity, assume:\n\n- sUSDM amount = `1e12`\n- price = `1e18`\n- price offset = `1e18`\n- USDC decimals = `6`\n- sUSDM decimals = `6`\n\nThen the result is:\n\n`1e12 * 1e18 * 1e6 / (1e6 * 1e18) = 1e12 USDC`\n\n`1e12` USDC units is `1,000,000 USDC`.\n\nHowever, `1e12` sUSDM should represent 1 sUSDM, because sUSDM shares are 12 decimals. If `sUSDM.decimals()` returned 12, the result would be:\n\n`1e12 * 1e18 * 1e6 / (1e12 * 1e18) = 1e6 USDC`\n\n`1e6` USDC units is `1 USDC`.",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n    function test_submissionValidity() public {\n        uint8 decimals = susdm.decimals();\n        assert(decimals == 6);\n        assert(decimals != 12);\n    }\n```",
